  "investigation_notes": "Diagnosis: **insufficient_evidence**\n\nWhat is happening:\n- Application `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` [E1,E4] but its `/health` returns `503 unhealthy` [E2]. Uploads stopped working is consistent with unhealthy app, but unhealthy is a symptom, not root cause.\n- Database `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` and `healthy` [E1,E5], with repeated `pg_isready exit 0` and `health_status: healthy` [E6]. This rules out DB-down as current cause, but does not prove app-to-DB connectivity.\n- Both containers were re-created/started ~15:54:24-15:55:04 [E6], with `restart_count 0` [E4,E5], `oom_killed false` [E4,E5]. No crash-loop evidence.\n- Filesystem capacity is not full: `/srv/lab-data 9.0% used, 0.2% inode` [E7] and `/ 6.8% used` [E10]. Disk-full / inode-full ruled out.\n- App has bind mount `source /srv/lab-data -> /data rw true` [E4] and runs as `1000:1000` [E4], so uploads depend on host directory writability, which could not be verified.\n\nWhat is missing - no conclusion on cause possible:\n- App logs unavailable [E3,E12] and DB logs unavailable [E9], so application error for uploads/health failure was not seen.\n- Upload directory access check for `/srv/lab-data/uploads` unavailable [E8] and for `/srv/lab-data` unavailable [E11], so permission / ownership / writable status for user `1000:1000` [E4] was not seen.\n- Without logs and path_access, permission-denied vs DB-error vs other app error cannot be distinguished. Do not conclude a cause by elimination alone.\n\nBudget of 12 checks used. Repairs require human approval; no changes made.\n",
